1
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:16,360
THE SECRET WOMAN

2
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:24,400
2 YEARS LATER

3
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,040
BASED ON ANNA EKBERG'SDEN
<i>HEMMELIGE KVINDE</i>

4
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,280
Have you checked the nets yet? Good.

5
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,039
-Hi!
-Ah, it's the Danish girl.

6
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,520
Morning, Louise.

7
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,119
-Here you go.
-Wow!

8
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,120
Lovely.

9
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,120
Wow.

10
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:40,159
Tell me, how's your mum?

11
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,680
-Better.
-Yeah?

12
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:46,280
Well, as soon as she's well enough,
come for some hot chocolate at the café.

13
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,999
-Okay?
-Okay.

14
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,720
Balder?

15
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,440
-Eight hundred kroner?
-Yep.

16
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,959
-Say hi to your mum.
-Sure.

17
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,080
See you soon.

18
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,760
-Morning.
-Hi.

19
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:11,760
Oi.

20
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,400
All right, what do we have here?

21
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,799
Oh, perfect!

22
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,599
-Huh?
-Oh, lovely!

23
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,199
-Let's put crab on our specials.
-Uh-huh.

24
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,680
-Okay. Thanks.
-I'll put them in the kitchen.

25
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,599
CRIME SCENE DO NOT CROSS
SERIAL KILLERS

26
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,960
A COMPLETE GUIDE
TO POLICE PROCEDURE

27
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,520
Hmm.

28
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:07,479
Good morning.

29
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,599
-Hi.
-Late night?

30
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,399
Did I wake you?

31
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:15,119
-No. No, not at all.
-Are you sure?

32
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,079
Mm.

33
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,079
Get any writing done?
Or did you get distracted?

34
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:20,279
I don't know what to say.

35
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,679
-The pyramids again?
-No.

36
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,919
No?

37
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:24,439
It was worse than that, in fact.

38
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:28,519
I went down a... a rabbit hole
with Mount Kailash, right.

39
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:31,199
It's a sacred mountain in Tibet actually.

40
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,119
-Mm-hmm.
-There are lots of stories...

41
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,199
about all these
temporal distortion things.

42
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:39,199
-I love you, you nerd!
-There's more to it.

43
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:41,599
-Mm.
-There are conspiracy theories...

44
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,679
Seriously.

45
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,359
We're now arriving
at the island of Tysnes.

46
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:50,759
A small island
with only 2,400 inhabitants,

47
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:54,639
but one with deep roots in Norse history.

48
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:56,639
Around the island you will find sites

49
00:04:56,640 --> 00:05:00,240
of great cultural
and historical importance.

50
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,960
Let me know
if you need anything.

51
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,119
Thank you, Maria.

52
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,479
-You're welcome. Say hi to your folks.
-Yeah, I will.

53
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,640
-See you.
-Bye.

54
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:21,039
-Louise?
-Mm?

55
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:23,879
That guy sitting there
won't stop staring at you.

56
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,879
But you are gorgeous,
so I don't blame him.

57
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,079
Ooh, well he's coming over here.

58
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,360
-Oh, great.
-Mm.

59
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,199
Helene?

60
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,279
It's me, Peter.

61
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,079
We, uh, worked at the same company.

62
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,440
Uh, sorry, but I'm not Helene.

63
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:43,920
-Hmm... What do you mean?
-My name's Louise.

64
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,320
This is me.

65
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,200
Louise Andersen.

66
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,239
-My apologies.
-No worries at all.

67
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:55,000
You must have a doppelgänger.

68
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:04,599
Congratulations
to Joachim and Louise. Cheers.

69
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:07,279
Here we go. Dinner's served!

70
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,639
-Ooh.
-Enjoy.

71
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,239
Time for me
to make a speech, I'm afraid.

72
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,959
Okay. Um, yeah.

73
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,879
We are engaged. She said yes.

74
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:22,839
I'm pleased to say, finally.
Um, it's a very cheap ring, I'm afraid.

75
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,000
We've been here
almost two years now.

76
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:32,319
And I've never felt more at home as,
um, I do here with you.

77
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,839
Aw, you're welcome.

78
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:34,840
Thank you.

79
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,840
Um, Louise...

80
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:41,120
Um, you are a magical person.

81
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,959
Mysterious. And magical.

82
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:52,119
And I feel like I've spent
a lot of time thinking about all of my...

83
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,239
silly, uh, little books

84
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:57,479
and the never-ending mountain
of boring research. Uh...

85
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,080
As if that was all that mattered.

86
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:01,800
But not any more.

87
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:05,280
You bring meaning to my life.

88
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,240
Every day.

89
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,120
And I adore you.

90
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,519
I love you.

91
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:24,599
Right, time for you to raise your glass.
To both of you, and love.

92
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,679
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

93
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,600
Cheers, everyone!

94
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,760
-Who is it?
-Him again?

95
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,999
Who?

96
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,599
Uh, there was a Danish man at the café
who wouldn't stop staring at Louise today.

97
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:42,759
He thought I was someone he knew, but...

98
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,039
Oh, yeah?

99
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:45,960
I'd rather not talk to him again.

100
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,640
I'll make sure he gets the message.

101
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,519
Yes?

102
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,639
Hi. I'd like to speak to Helene.

103
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:00,640
Yeah, well, sorry, there's no one
called Helene here, I'm afraid.

104
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:04,359
Look, I have something
very important to tell her.

105
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,600
It's about her past, okay?

106
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,999
As I said you're, uh...

107
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,960
You're barking up the wrong tree,
I would say. So...

108
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,520
Okay.

109
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,279
He was obnoxious.

110
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,720
-Yes.
-And you've never seen the guy before?

111
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,640
I don't think. Um...

112
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:38,919
I don't remember seeing him before, um...
I don't think so, but, erm...

113
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:41,639
Hey. What is it?

114
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:44,599
Is there something
that's coming back to you?

115
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,320
Nothing, he just made me...

116
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,760
scared.

117
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:59,040
Louise, If he's somehow managed
to jog your memory...

118
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:05,000
If you're starting to remember...
you can tell me. We'll figure things out.

119
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:07,600
Yeah.

120
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:11,880
Thank you.

121
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:19,320
-Let's sleep now.
-Mm.

122
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:30,760
Wow.

123
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:55,559
I'VE GONE TO THE MAINLAND. I'LL BE BACK
ON THE LAST FERRY THIS AFTERNOON.

124
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,960
I LOVE YOU!

125
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:09,319
<i>Okay, Louise. You've come
because you're unsure of your identity?</i>

126
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,239
Yes.

127
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:14,039
I see. And your file says that
just over two years ago,

128
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:17,039
you were found unconscious at the harbour?

129
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:21,159
Yes. Well, um, I was on a ship,
when it came into the harbour.

130
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,919
And you had, uh, serious injuries?

131
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:29,439
Yeah. Yeah, to my neck,
my head, an arm, and my ribs.

132
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:33,760
And you've no idea how you managed
to board the ship, is what it says here?

133
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,840
No.

134
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:38,520
<i>I was in hospital
for a long time.</i>

135
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
<i>Um...</i>

136
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:44,519
And the doctors
then diagnosed me with amnesia.

137
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:46,519
Then how did the doctors know
who you were?

138
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:48,119
I still had my bag

139
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,120
with a few belongings and my ID.

140
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,039
<i>So they told me who I was.</i>

141
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:55,559
-Louise Andersen?
-Yeah.

142
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:59,999
And so the Danish police just accepted
the fact that you were Louise Andersen?

143
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,800
Yes, they did, because
I said that they were right.

144
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:10,760
I told them I was Louise
and my memories were coming back to me.

145
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
And were they?

146
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:16,879
No, um, I had no idea who I was.

147
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,439
Why didn't you say that?

148
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:22,560
Because... It's hard to explain,
but I was afraid.

149
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,800
It's frightening not to know who you are...

150
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:30,319
I guess I hoped that I was her.

151
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:31,799
And you left it at that?

152
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:36,479
No. I searched for myself online.
There was nothing though.

153
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:39,719
-Nothing?
-There are many Louise Andersens.

154
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:42,759
And the police?
No one contacted family or anything?

155
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:44,199
Well, I didn't have one.

156
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,600
No next of kin?

157
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:51,279
No. It turned out
I'd... I'd lived a... a hard life.

158
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:55,360
The only records the police had of me were
a couple of arrests in Copenhagen for...

159
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,320
for prostitution.

160
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:05,279
I... I have a feeling
I must've been on the run back then.

161
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:09,600
So I came here
to find out who I am and what happened.

162
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,280
Right.

163
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,520
We'll do a DNA test.

164
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,920
<i>Your real name
is Helene Söderberg.</i>

165
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:27,039
You disappeared
from your family in Denmark

166
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,040
just over two years ago.

167
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:33,120
The Danish police
have been looking for you ever since.

168
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,800
A lot of people have been looking for you.

169
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,840
And you're married.

170
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,120
You have a son.

171
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,600
A son?

172
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:10,560
-Hi. Joachim Bjørndal? Iben Rask.
-Hi. Yes.

173
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,840
Can you explain it again?

174
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:18,759
Because she had an ID
when she was found,

175
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:22,360
unfortunately they didn't investigate
the matter any further.

176
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,400
And she confirmed to them
that she was Louise Andersen.

177
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,399
And where... Where is Louise?

178
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:34,720
Oh, wait.
I guess she isn't Louise, is she?

179
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:38,799
No. Helene's now in the care
of the crisis team.

180
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:42,039
You can see her if you like,
but just to reiterate, Joachim...

181
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:44,280
It's definitely her.

182
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,360
The DNA test proved it.

183
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:50,360
We contacted the Danish police
and it's been verified.

184
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:53,600
And we've also notified
her family in Denmark.

185
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,800
Her family?

186
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:09,439
Apologies. A shorter last name
would've made life easier.

187
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,199
Mr. Söderberg? Sorry to interrupt.

188
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,760
-Yes?
-Um, it's urgent I'm afraid.

189
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,160
Ah. Excuse me.

190
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,079
He'll be right back.

191
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,080
Yes?

192
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:34,920
Yes?

193
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:46,039
Did you speak to the police?

194
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:49,720
Yeah. They've explained it all to me, so...

195
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,120
It'll be okay.

196
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,599
I think Helene's a beautiful name.

197
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:02,240
Well, we'll work through it.

198
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:07,360
I must go and meet them.

199
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,280
Yeah.

200
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,120
I have a child.

201
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,560
I'm someone's mother.

202
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:23,680
I have to go to Denmark
and figure out what happened.

203
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,360
You're right. Mm.

204
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:28,160
I understand.

205
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:31,800
But you know this doesn't change anything.

206
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:35,520
You and I are getting married.

207
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:10,880
{\an8}WELCOME TO COPENHAGEN

208
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:16,599
Now then. Are you excited?

209
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,679
I am, yeah.

210
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,680
Mm?

211
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,640
You look wonderful.

212
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:28,480
-Let me see you.
-Okay.

213
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,839
You take it easy. Don't blame her.

214
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,519
You know she's been through
a terrible ordeal.

215
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,320
I'm sure it must be hard for her.

216
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,440
We're here, Mrs Söderberg.

217
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:53,640
Is that her?

218
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:57,080
Yes. I presume.

219
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:26,719
Hi.

220
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,080
-Hi.
-Welcome.

221
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:35,840
Uh, don't you want to say hi
to your mother, Alexander?

222
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:37,440
You wanna say hi?

223
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:40,880
-Don't you want to say hello?
-Hmm?

224
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:44,239
-Alexander?
-I'll go after him.

225
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,520
Right. Um, this is my mother.

226
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:48,479
Yeah.

227
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,560
Caroline.

228
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:57,560
It is so good to have you home again.

229
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,120
-Uh, will you go check on him?
-Of course.

230
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,080
I'm sure he'll come around.

231
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:13,679
And then there's me, uh... I'm Edmund.

232
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,399
-Um...
-I guessed you... you were.

233
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:20,639
-It's... It's all a... a bit awkward.
-Yes.

234
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,080
Mm.

235
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,039
You'll come inside?

236
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,960
Yes. Okay.

237
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,439
I can take your things.

238
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,599
Thanks.

239
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:32,719
Go on in.

240
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:40,360
This is your childhood home.
You grew up here with your father.

241
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:42,960
And that's you and him.

242
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:55,560
This is the piano room.
You used to play here as a child.

243
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:03,600
And in here
was your father's study.

244
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,439
You don't recognise anything?

245
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,039
No, not really.

246
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:23,319
Well, um, they said to expect that.

247
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:26,399
I had hoped that
when you saw Alexander and me,

248
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:30,080
you know, things might begin to...
...come back.

249
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:33,560
Well, the psychologists hope so.

250
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,280
I hope so too.

251
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,840
Thank you.

252
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,920
What happened when I disappeared?

253
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:55,759
Just before you vanished,
your father passed.

254
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:59,800
The man hadn't been well at all.
He went downhill very rapidly and you...

255
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:03,880
you took care of him.
But it was very intense.

256
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:08,680
His passing brought out
a sort of dark bleakness in you.

257
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,600
You had been on medications...

258
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:15,200
And I think it's possible
you stopped taking them.

259
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:19,319
So you were just spiralling.

260
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,920
And then you disappeared.
I spent months looking for you.

261
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:27,999
But in all my searching,
I never had the thought to look abroad,

262
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,400
which I will always regret.

263
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:33,760
Helene, this isn't easy
for me to say, but...

264
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:39,280
In the end I told myself
that you had ended it all.

265
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,119
It was an option you'd mentioned before.

266
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:50,319
Oh... I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to bring all this up.

267
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:52,679
It wasn't my intention
to drag up all that...

268
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:55,080
-Uh...
-No, I was the one asking, don't worry.

269
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:56,840
Sorry.

270
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:01,759
Do you... Do you think I could, um...
maybe talk to him?

271
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:06,440
Oh yes, sure. Uh, right.
Up the stairs, first door on your right.

272
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,520
-Thanks.
-Yeah.

273
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:15,119
Alexander?

274
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,680
You don't remember me?

275
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,680
I will, eventually.

276
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,680
Did you miss me?

277
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:59,480
Yeah. I did, in my heart.

278
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,160
I'm here now.

279
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:09,960
I won't go away again. Okay?

280
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,400
Mm.

281
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,960
Oh, Alexander...

282
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:26,880
You never call me Alexander.

283
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:30,560
Then what do I call you?

284
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,200
You really don't know it?

285
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:38,960
I'm trying.

286
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:45,880
<i>Duckling.</i>

287
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:49,480
Duckling.

288
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,560
Of course.

289
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:11,839
<i>Hi, this is Iben Rask.</i>

290
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:15,639
Hi, hi. It's Joachim.
I recently spoke to you at the hospital.

291
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:17,319
Oh, hi, Joachim.

292
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:19,119
-<i>Hello.</i>
-How is everything?

293
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:23,079
I just find it a bit strange.
Something's not right.

294
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:25,999
Is that
the crime writer in you talking?

295
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:30,839
No, I mean... Have you tried looking up
her name online? Helene Söderberg?

296
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:32,599
Yes, I did try that.

297
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:34,160
<i>And what did you find?</i>

298
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:38,679
-Yeah, I didn't find too much.
<i>-Exactly. Nothing.</i>

299
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:41,399
I've been searching
for four hours and not a thing.

300
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:44,479
No social media, nothing. It's odd.

301
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:46,839
<i>Yeah, I have to say,
I don't disagree with you there.</i>

302
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:51,319
And then there's her new identity...
This other woman's stolen identity...

303
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:53,919
The real Louise.
What about her? Where is she?

304
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:56,920
Look, her case has already gone over
to the Danish police.

305
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:00,440
So is there...

306
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,839
A contact, or someone
I could speak to over there?

307
00:25:03,840 --> 00:25:04,840
<i>Yes.</i>

308
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,720
Your grandma's on her way.

309
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:12,639
Good night.

310
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:13,720
Good night.

311
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:42,560
Helene?

312
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:02,560
Is he sleeping?

313
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:05,160
No.

314
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:08,120
But he let me read to him.

315
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:11,679
Your mother's with him now
until he falls asleep.

316
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:12,959
Right.

317
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:15,319
He's been a little more, um...

318
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:18,160
Mm... Anxious after you vanished.

319
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,520
Um, this wine...

320
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,240
It's one of your favourites.

321
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:27,839
Well it used to be a favourite.

322
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:30,000
Ah.

323
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:35,919
A toast.

324
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:36,920
A toast.

325
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,879
Do you like it?

326
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:43,880
Mm.

327
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:50,559
Um, how long have we been married?

328
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:55,519
Sorry, they probably said already
but it's such a blur.

329
00:26:55,520 --> 00:26:57,440
-It's eight years now.
-Woah.

330
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,919
And how did we meet each other?

331
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:04,759
I worked in your father's business,
uh, and that's where we both worked.

332
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:08,679
And well now... we run the company.

333
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:10,719
We're both on the board of directors.

334
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:13,760
In, um, shipping... I've been told?

335
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:15,239
Yeah, shipping.

336
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:18,680
We are the fourth-largest
shipping firm in the North.

337
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:27,479
So, what do I do there?

338
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:30,239
Uh... Um...

339
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:35,239
You were our CFO.
You were very good. Very sharp.

340
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:37,439
-So, in finance?
-Yes.

341
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,200
-That's what I did?
-Mm-hmm.

342
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:43,640
-I run a café on the island.
-Mm.

343
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:47,279
That's why business and accounting came
really easily to me, I suppose.

344
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:48,520
-Well, there you go.
-Mm.

345
00:27:55,520 --> 00:27:58,679
Um, I don't run it alone. The café. I...

346
00:28:00,040 --> 00:28:03,079
I run it with my boyfriend.
Well, my fiancé.

347
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:06,000
Yep, I know. Um... yeah.

348
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:07,960
Joachim.

349
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:10,440
Yeah.

350
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,600
I see that you're um...

351
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:14,880
You're wearing his ring?

352
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:20,960
Yes. Do you mind?

353
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:26,480
I'm just glad you're back home again.

354
00:28:27,680 --> 00:28:30,720
And I'm glad
that Alexander has his mother back.

355
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:36,280
Um, and then, then rest
we'll just make work somehow, right?

356
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:39,360
-Yeah.
-But...

357
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:43,080
I'd really like to show you something.
Bring your wine.

358
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:45,560
-Come on.
-Okay.

359
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:50,760
It's a small film we had made
for you for your birthday a few years ago.

360
00:28:52,840 --> 00:28:53,880
It's your story.

361
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:56,799
<i>-Hi!</i>
<i>-Hi.</i>

362
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:01,759
<i>I'm flying!</i>

363
00:29:01,760 --> 00:29:05,320
You grew up here with your father
after your mother died.

364
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:10,080
She got cancer, sadly, when, um...
when you were very young.

365
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:16,599
But your father adored you,
and he gave you everything you wanted.

366
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:19,400
And you two were inseparable.

367
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:24,360
And you and I, we... we met at work.

368
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:26,560
Well, I...

369
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:31,639
I was so intimidated by you.
The boss's beautiful daughter.

370
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:38,600
But I won you over.
And we got married.

371
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:40,800
We were madly in love.

372
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:44,119
Nothing could keep us apart.

373
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:51,799
<i>Feel it, he's kicking now!</i>

374
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:55,400
And then our family was complete
when Alexander came along.

375
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:58,720
We were so happy.

376
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:04,240
<i>His little hands, his nose...</i>

377
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:29,720
Helene, you'll sleep
in the master bedroom, all right?

378
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:32,400
And I'll make up a guest room for Edmund.

379
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,000
I think it's the best option.

380
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,360
Wait, Caroline?

381
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:39,920
Yes?

382
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:43,640
Thank you for taking care of Alexander.

383
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:45,839
Oh, but of course.

384
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:49,119
It's truly been a joy.
He's honestly such a delight.

385
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:52,880
And, um...

386
00:30:57,600 --> 00:30:58,800
Was I a good mother?

387
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:08,240
You were just as you should be.

388
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:12,000
You listened to him. You adored him.

389
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:19,280
It’s just hard to believe
that I forgot about him.

390
00:31:21,320 --> 00:31:23,919
Or that I'd forget
giving birth to my child.

391
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:26,040
You really don't remember anything?

392
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:31,280
-A few things here and there.
-Well, there you go.

393
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:35,880
Your head's playing tricks on you
but your heart remembered him.

394
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,160
Don't blame yourself.

395
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:42,800
You're here now.

396
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:45,920
Sleep well.

397
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:48,080
You too.

398
00:32:10,280 --> 00:32:11,439
<i>Hi.</i>

399
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:12,480
Hi.

400
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:15,640
Go on. What's going on?

401
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:19,360
It's... intense.

402
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:21,720
I can imagine.

403
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:27,680
But what's it like there?
Are they... nice? Looking after you?

404
00:32:28,560 --> 00:32:31,079
<i>It's... really big here.</i>

405
00:32:31,080 --> 00:32:32,680
And grand.

406
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:36,960
They seem good. And there's Alexander.

407
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:40,280
Yeah.

408
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:47,480
But have you found out
any more answers, or information?

409
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:50,759
<i>That's why you went to Denmark, isn't it?</i>

410
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:55,719
Yeah. No, right now,
I'm just trying to navigate it all.

411
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:58,999
<i>Right, but what happened
when you disappeared?</i>

412
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:01,839
<i>You have to find out how you ended up
on that ship to Norway.</i>

413
00:33:01,840 --> 00:33:03,080
Joachim, I...

414
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:09,839
It will have to wait.

415
00:33:09,840 --> 00:33:16,760
<i>I can't handle anymore right now.
I'm going to need some more time, okay?</i>

416
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:19,160
Yeah, all right.

417
00:33:22,120 --> 00:33:23,200
I love you.

418
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:26,279
I love you.

419
00:33:26,280 --> 00:33:28,240
<i>I'll be in touch, okay? Bye.</i>

420
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:58,240
-Bye, Grandma.
-Bye, darling. Bye.

421
00:33:58,880 --> 00:34:00,040
See you.

422
00:34:09,160 --> 00:34:10,439
Hi, David.

423
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:11,600
Hi, Alexander.

424
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:14,279
Look, this is my mum.

425
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:16,879
-What's your name?
-I'm Helene.

426
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:18,159
She's been home for two days.

427
00:34:18,160 --> 00:34:19,679
-Hi! Hello.
-Ooh.

428
00:34:19,680 --> 00:34:22,079
Hello there! Your friends?

429
00:34:22,080 --> 00:34:25,079
-Have you been to the school before?
-No, I haven't.

430
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:26,679
-I've been to Norway too.
-Okay.

431
00:34:26,680 --> 00:34:27,959
It's so beautiful.

432
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:30,079
Bye, Mum.

433
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:33,199
All right, duckling. Have a good day.
Okay, sweetheart?

434
00:34:33,200 --> 00:34:35,360
-See you.
-Have a nice day, Mum!

435
00:34:45,240 --> 00:34:47,080
Are you sure you're ready, Helene?

436
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:52,400
Yeah. I'm hoping
it will help me remember.

437
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:53,800
Okay.

438
00:34:58,440 --> 00:35:00,239
Hi, Helene. I'm glad you're back.

439
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:01,440
Hmm. Thanks.

440
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,159
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

441
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:07,319
Hi, Helene. So good to see you again.

442
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:08,399
-Good morning.
-Thanks.

443
00:35:08,400 --> 00:35:09,600
Beautiful flowers.

444
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:16,199
Are you okay?

445
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:21,039
Uh... That man... The one over there
looks a lot like the man who...

446
00:35:21,040 --> 00:35:22,479
saw me in Norway.

447
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:25,919
Oh, well it is him.
He works in our compliance department.

448
00:35:25,920 --> 00:35:29,720
He was on holiday in Norway
when he saw you. Luckily for us.

449
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:32,639
Welcome back, Helene.

450
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:33,640
Thank you.

451
00:35:44,560 --> 00:35:47,680
This is the last known photo
of Louise Andersen.

452
00:35:48,320 --> 00:35:52,399
We sent that photo to the Norwegian police
and they identified her, so...

453
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:53,799
Well, that was that.

454
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:57,679
Okay, but who is she, right?
I mean, who is Louise Andersen?

455
00:35:57,680 --> 00:36:01,080
We have very little on Louise Andersen
other than she was a prostitute.

456
00:36:01,680 --> 00:36:02,879
We've listed her as missing,

457
00:36:02,880 --> 00:36:05,759
but people in that world
tend to disappear.

458
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:08,520
It's just... do you think they look alike?

459
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:10,879
Do you think Helene and Louise look alike?

460
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:12,719
-I'd say a little.
-Oh.

461
00:36:12,720 --> 00:36:15,679
Height, hair colour, eye colour.

462
00:36:15,680 --> 00:36:18,919
But most importantly, the officers
involved had no reason to suspect

463
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:21,879
that the woman on the ID wasn't her
when they found her.

464
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:24,119
Okay. But so, Helene Söderberg, then...

465
00:36:24,120 --> 00:36:26,319
Why didn't you do a bigger search
when she went missing?

466
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:28,119
Well, there weren't many leads.

467
00:36:28,120 --> 00:36:32,000
And our information suggested that
she had committed suicide.

468
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,160
What information?

469
00:36:35,640 --> 00:36:36,840
A history of mental illness.

470
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:39,239
Helene Söderberg
was suffering from psychosis

471
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:41,560
when she disappeared. Severe psychosis.

472
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:52,080
Hello, Mrs Söderberg.

473
00:36:53,280 --> 00:36:55,599
So, Edmund showed you to your old office?

474
00:36:55,600 --> 00:36:56,600
Yes.

475
00:36:59,560 --> 00:37:00,600
Ingrid.

476
00:37:02,480 --> 00:37:04,559
You don't recognise me?

477
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:05,640
No, sorry.

478
00:37:06,520 --> 00:37:08,919
Well... Well,
I suppose we'll just start over.

479
00:37:08,920 --> 00:37:12,079
Ingrid Jensen.
I was your secretary before.

480
00:37:12,080 --> 00:37:14,079
And you also worked for my father?

481
00:37:14,080 --> 00:37:18,880
Yes. Until he fell sick and then you...
then you took over.

482
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,440
Uh, so...

483
00:37:21,360 --> 00:37:24,239
I'm so sorry, they said that if we were...

484
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:28,799
if we were talking of the past,
then we must be careful with it.

485
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,639
Oh, please don't worry, it's no problem.

486
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:34,159
I'm actually trying to remember
as much as possible.

487
00:37:34,160 --> 00:37:35,160
Mm.

488
00:37:36,200 --> 00:37:38,680
Ah, well in that case...

489
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:43,320
Why don't you look in here.

490
00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:47,639
It's an anniversary book celebrating
the first ten years of the company.

491
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:48,680
Okay.

492
00:37:51,120 --> 00:37:52,360
SÖDERBERG SHIPPING
1967-1977

493
00:38:00,240 --> 00:38:02,959
Well, I've brought you
a little of everything.

494
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:05,719
Annual reports and financial statements.

495
00:38:05,720 --> 00:38:08,159
Don't worry, you won't need
to approve anything here.

496
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:11,640
It's just to give you an idea.
We'll ease you back in.

497
00:38:17,960 --> 00:38:21,159
-The first pages are...
-The management figures.

498
00:38:21,160 --> 00:38:22,520
That's correct.

499
00:38:27,080 --> 00:38:29,080
I see you remember a few things, huh?

500
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:32,800
Yeah.

501
00:38:47,680 --> 00:38:48,999
POLICE
WANTED AND MISSING PERSONS

502
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:50,840
MISSING SINCE 2024.
LAST SEEN AROUND HALMTORVET

503
00:38:53,640 --> 00:38:54,799
MISSING SINCE 2024

504
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:56,600
{\an8}SLENDER BUILD, LONG DARK HAIR

505
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:07,520
{\an8}TRANSPORT AND LOGISTICS LEADER

506
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:10,039
WHO ARE WE?

507
00:39:10,040 --> 00:39:11,039
HISTORY

508
00:39:11,040 --> 00:39:13,360
{\an8}AKSEL SÖDERBERG FOUNDED SÖDERBERG SHIPPING
IN 1967.

509
00:39:17,720 --> 00:39:18,720
IMAGES

510
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:30,800
NO RESULTS FOR YOUR SEARCH

511
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:56,840
Hi. Um, do you have any articles
featuring... these keywords?

512
00:39:57,320 --> 00:39:58,480
Let me look.

513
00:40:05,600 --> 00:40:08,560
-Nothing?
-No, no results, sorry.

514
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:10,840
Do you hold originals here?

515
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:14,919
I'll see what I can find.

516
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:16,920
-Thanks, I'll wait.
-You're welcome.

517
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:19,839
Come get me!

518
00:40:19,840 --> 00:40:21,359
Go!

519
00:40:21,360 --> 00:40:22,720
Come here, you!

520
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:25,440
Right.

521
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:29,600
Gotcha!

522
00:40:33,840 --> 00:40:36,800
-No, no, no. Stop!
-You're it!

523
00:40:37,760 --> 00:40:40,120
Oh, Alexander.

524
00:40:40,720 --> 00:40:42,199
-Ready?
-We're ready.

525
00:40:42,200 --> 00:40:43,480
-Ready?
-Yes.

526
00:40:44,480 --> 00:40:46,760
You got it? Oh, it's mine.

527
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:49,759
We got him!

528
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:52,039
-You got him!
-Come on, Dad.

529
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:53,919
-We got him.
-No!

530
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:55,840
-Yeah, we did!
-Watch out! He's up!

531
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:02,559
-Yeah!
-Well done.

532
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:04,759
-Hold on, hold on, hold on.
-High five!

533
00:41:04,760 --> 00:41:06,839
-Yeah.
-Nice work.

534
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:08,599
Uh, I need to get this.

535
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:09,959
No, Dad...

536
00:41:09,960 --> 00:41:11,840
Hello?

537
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:14,360
Your shoelace is untied.

538
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:19,240
-You're good at tennis.
-Thanks.

539
00:41:20,720 --> 00:41:22,719
Are you still mad at Dad?

540
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:23,720
Mad how?

541
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:28,160
You screamed at him
right before you disappeared.

542
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:31,400
You were there?

543
00:41:32,040 --> 00:41:34,320
Yes. It was at night.

544
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:42,720
Look, parents do argue.
I'm sure there was no need to worry.

545
00:41:44,240 --> 00:41:46,000
You were arguing over me.

546
00:41:47,240 --> 00:41:49,160
None of this is your fault.

547
00:41:51,680 --> 00:41:52,760
You know that?

548
00:41:56,480 --> 00:41:57,559
Okay.

549
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:03,839
Mm. Can I taste it?

550
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:05,320
Mm-hmm. Try it.

551
00:42:07,200 --> 00:42:08,960
-Delicious, isn't it?
-Mm.

552
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:15,800
I made you this
on our very first date.

553
00:42:16,440 --> 00:42:17,440
Mm.

554
00:43:10,640 --> 00:43:11,920
I've missed you, Helene.

555
00:43:48,640 --> 00:43:51,839
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

556
00:43:54,960 --> 00:43:55,960
I'm sorry.

557
00:44:03,480 --> 00:44:06,960
-I... I didn't mean...
-No, no, it's all right.

558
00:44:09,120 --> 00:44:11,200
You aren't ready. It's fine.

559
00:44:35,640 --> 00:44:36,839
Come here.

560
00:46:42,080 --> 00:46:44,560
Listen. It's important.

561
00:46:54,200 --> 00:46:56,719
Helene? All okay?

562
00:46:56,720 --> 00:46:59,200
Yeah.

563
00:47:00,320 --> 00:47:02,280
You should be asleep.

564
00:47:02,920 --> 00:47:05,400
My father was up here, wasn't he?

565
00:47:06,240 --> 00:47:08,600
He moved to the tower room
when he got sick.

566
00:47:09,320 --> 00:47:11,319
He wanted a view of the forest.

567
00:47:11,320 --> 00:47:13,360
You said it soothed him.

568
00:47:14,080 --> 00:47:15,240
Do you know...

569
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:20,879
What he said to me, at the end?
I mean, right before he died?

570
00:47:20,880 --> 00:47:26,000
No, I don't know, my dear.
I didn't know your father all that well.

571
00:47:28,400 --> 00:47:30,520
SUSPICIOUS DEATH
DIED IN HIS OWN HOME

572
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:35,079
-Where did you get these?
-National Library.

573
00:47:35,080 --> 00:47:36,079
Mm-hmm.

574
00:47:36,080 --> 00:47:39,600
All the digital archives were erased.
Which is a bit weird, don't you think?

575
00:47:40,200 --> 00:47:42,159
So I had to make copies
from the actual newspapers.

576
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:43,879
Right.

577
00:47:43,880 --> 00:47:45,760
And how can I help, then?

578
00:47:47,800 --> 00:47:50,240
Well, I want to know
if you ever looked into that?

579
00:47:51,440 --> 00:47:52,559
What exactly?

580
00:47:52,560 --> 00:47:55,919
About...
Helen's father. The way he died.

581
00:47:55,920 --> 00:47:58,079
Well, it says he was found dead at home.

582
00:47:58,080 --> 00:48:01,240
We looked into it,
but concluded that it was an accident.

583
00:48:02,120 --> 00:48:03,559
There's no more to that case.

584
00:48:03,560 --> 00:48:05,040
Yeah, but I have more evidence.

585
00:48:06,680 --> 00:48:08,679
Louise... Um, Helene...

586
00:48:08,680 --> 00:48:12,400
Helene was found aboard a ship.
This ship here.

587
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:15,759
Did any of you look into
how she came to be aboard that ship?

588
00:48:15,760 --> 00:48:20,440
You mean how she got on board
a Norwegian ship several years ago?

589
00:48:21,680 --> 00:48:23,959
There's no way I could know that.

590
00:48:23,960 --> 00:48:26,360
No, I understand that, but...

591
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:30,000
I can feel it. There's more going on.

592
00:48:30,680 --> 00:48:32,880
I know it. So will you help me?

593
00:48:35,440 --> 00:48:38,800
I expect she boarded
from one of the harbours along its route.

594
00:48:39,320 --> 00:48:43,240
If I were you, I'd locate the ship's log
and then you can check the route it took.

595
00:48:44,040 --> 00:48:45,679
There's nothing else we can do.

596
00:48:48,160 --> 00:48:50,400
Ten, thirty...

597
00:48:51,440 --> 00:48:53,439
What about that one? What is it?

598
00:48:53,440 --> 00:48:55,639
Alexander, we need to go.
Can you get ready?

599
00:48:55,640 --> 00:48:56,680
Okay.

600
00:48:58,760 --> 00:49:00,560
Yeah. Off you go.

601
00:49:05,240 --> 00:49:06,240
Good morning.

602
00:49:09,880 --> 00:49:11,080
I'll check on him.

603
00:49:16,880 --> 00:49:18,760
Your mother seems so wonderful, Edmund.

604
00:49:20,840 --> 00:49:23,799
I'm glad she was with Alexander
while I was away.

605
00:49:23,800 --> 00:49:24,920
Yes.

606
00:49:26,280 --> 00:49:27,880
By the way, I was thinking...

607
00:49:28,960 --> 00:49:32,599
We haven't really spoken about
my father, you know?

608
00:49:32,600 --> 00:49:34,040
How he died.

609
00:49:35,840 --> 00:49:40,680
You and Alexander were alone
in the house that day.

610
00:49:41,840 --> 00:49:44,520
And no one really knows what happened.

611
00:49:45,120 --> 00:49:48,559
But we think he might have been trying
to leave his room

612
00:49:48,560 --> 00:49:51,520
and he fell... down the stairs.

613
00:49:54,440 --> 00:49:56,599
So it was me who found him or...?

614
00:49:56,600 --> 00:50:00,199
Yes.
I've been withholding the details.

615
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:03,080
It was violently traumatising for you.

616
00:50:05,160 --> 00:50:09,399
My darling, I don't want you to go back
to that dark place again.

617
00:50:20,880 --> 00:50:23,880
{\an8}OUR EMPLOYEES PHOTOGRAPHED
IN FRONT OF THE OFFICES ON WILDERS STREET

618
00:50:32,400 --> 00:50:35,719
Ingrid, how come there's pages missing?

619
00:50:35,720 --> 00:50:38,280
Oh. No idea.

620
00:50:40,200 --> 00:50:44,119
I've got another copy at home
from when I first began working here.

621
00:50:44,120 --> 00:50:45,920
I can see if they're in there,
if you'd like?

622
00:50:47,080 --> 00:50:49,480
That would be great. Thank you.

623
00:50:52,400 --> 00:50:54,280
-Um, Ingrid?
-Yeah?

624
00:50:56,520 --> 00:50:59,480
What was I doing before I disappeared?

625
00:51:00,160 --> 00:51:01,720
Uh... Uh...

626
00:51:03,160 --> 00:51:08,320
Uh... Oh, I think it's best if you...
talk to your husband about it, yes?

627
00:51:16,760 --> 00:51:19,320
It's only that I'd really like to know...

628
00:51:20,240 --> 00:51:22,440
your view of what... what happened.

629
00:51:26,320 --> 00:51:27,640
Uh, well...

630
00:51:28,760 --> 00:51:31,599
I can only really tell you
what you said to me.

631
00:51:31,600 --> 00:51:32,840
Mm-hmm.

632
00:51:34,840 --> 00:51:38,880
Well, he tried to speak to you about
something important right before he died.

633
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:44,360
On his deathbed, he drifted
in and out of consciousness, so...

634
00:51:45,080 --> 00:51:47,079
he would forget
what he'd already said to you,

635
00:51:47,080 --> 00:51:49,559
and so he ran out of time
to tell you it all.

636
00:51:51,680 --> 00:51:52,680
Hmm.

637
00:51:54,280 --> 00:52:00,079
And then right before you vanished...
it seemed like you were obsessed.

638
00:52:00,080 --> 00:52:02,520
How? What... What was I doing?

639
00:52:03,120 --> 00:52:06,640
You were convinced that he had...
a warning, a confession.

640
00:52:07,880 --> 00:52:10,519
That there was something
you needed to know before he died

641
00:52:10,520 --> 00:52:12,000
and you took over the company.

642
00:52:12,760 --> 00:52:16,840
Then, after he passed,
you combed through everything here.

643
00:52:17,680 --> 00:52:21,640
Contracts, transactions, every client,
all of the routes. I mean it.

644
00:52:22,240 --> 00:52:27,240
All of it. You became more and more...
It pains me to say it, but...

645
00:52:28,960 --> 00:52:31,800
you seemed manic, to tell the truth.

646
00:52:32,800 --> 00:52:34,320
You were working day and night.

647
00:52:35,560 --> 00:52:36,800
And what about Edmund?

648
00:52:38,280 --> 00:52:42,720
Edmund, he...
He tried to ease your mind.

649
00:52:43,920 --> 00:52:46,559
Reassure you it was okay.

650
00:52:46,560 --> 00:52:48,719
So that's why I disappeared.

651
00:52:48,720 --> 00:52:50,079
Uh... Sorry, I...

652
00:52:50,080 --> 00:52:54,400
I discovered something.
His death wasn't why I broke down.

653
00:52:56,040 --> 00:52:57,839
I can only say what I saw.

654
00:52:57,840 --> 00:52:58,840
Yes.

655
00:53:17,960 --> 00:53:21,999
Ingrid, I'd like to know precisely what
I was doing before I disappeared.

656
00:53:22,000 --> 00:53:23,840
What I was working on and who I met with.

657
00:53:24,400 --> 00:53:26,279
Yes. I'll find your old diary.

658
00:53:26,280 --> 00:53:27,639
Thanks.

659
00:53:27,640 --> 00:53:30,720
I do remember one thing though.
Your last meeting was with the bank.

660
00:53:31,400 --> 00:53:34,320
You were saying
that meeting was important to you...

661
00:53:35,160 --> 00:53:36,959
Yes, I remember finding it strange

662
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:39,279
that you weren't meeting with
Söderberg's branch

663
00:53:39,280 --> 00:53:41,199
who we dealt with normally.

664
00:53:41,200 --> 00:53:42,119
Okay.

665
00:53:42,120 --> 00:53:45,199
Okay. Could you find the name of the bank,
and my calendar?

666
00:53:45,200 --> 00:53:46,320
Of course.

667
00:53:50,240 --> 00:53:51,919
-Mrs Söderberg?
-Hi.

668
00:53:51,920 --> 00:53:54,239
It's been a while.
Good to see you again.

669
00:53:54,240 --> 00:53:55,240
Likewise.

670
00:53:56,600 --> 00:53:58,680
So, how can we help you today?

671
00:53:59,600 --> 00:54:01,520
-When I last was here, um...
-Mm.

672
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:04,240
What did I say to you?

673
00:54:04,840 --> 00:54:08,240
Uh, do you mean when you set up
your safe-deposit box?

674
00:54:09,080 --> 00:54:11,160
Yeah. That time.

675
00:54:12,200 --> 00:54:14,120
Yeah, what exactly was our agreement?

676
00:54:14,680 --> 00:54:16,799
Well,
there was no agreement as such.

677
00:54:16,800 --> 00:54:19,360
You just set up a safe-deposit box.

678
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:22,000
And you didn't want your husband to know.

679
00:54:24,560 --> 00:54:26,040
That was it, yeah.

680
00:54:48,880 --> 00:54:51,200
PRENUPTIAL AGREEMENT

681
00:55:20,800 --> 00:55:23,399
-Yes, Ingrid?
<i>-I found your old calendar.</i>

682
00:55:23,400 --> 00:55:24,519
And?

683
00:55:24,520 --> 00:55:26,239
<i>In the days before you disappeared,</i>

684
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:29,079
<i>you had a meeting
with someone called Elisabeth Fauerskov.</i>

685
00:55:29,080 --> 00:55:31,079
-<i>Does that ring a bell?</i>
-Not at all.

686
00:55:31,080 --> 00:55:35,679
<i>She was the CEO of
one of our sub-contractors, JM Shipping.</i>

687
00:55:35,680 --> 00:55:37,959
<i>And I believe she knew your husband.</i>

688
00:55:37,960 --> 00:55:39,119
Okay?

689
00:55:39,120 --> 00:55:42,119
<i>-Anyway, I'm sending you her details now.</i>
-Okay. Thanks for that.

690
00:55:42,120 --> 00:55:43,400
-Right, bye.
-Thank you.

691
00:55:54,520 --> 00:55:58,439
-<i>Elisabeth Fauerskov.</i>
-Hi, Elisabeth. I am Helene Söderberg.

692
00:55:58,440 --> 00:56:00,919
-I'm calling to speak...
<i>-I... I don't want to talk to you.</i>

693
00:56:00,920 --> 00:56:03,240
<i>Don't contact me.</i>

694
00:56:44,240 --> 00:56:46,440
SHIP ROUTE INFO

695
00:56:56,120 --> 00:56:59,120
FYKSESUND BRIDGE

696
00:57:16,040 --> 00:57:18,799
Charlie's not my dad,
he's more like...

697
00:57:18,800 --> 00:57:20,839
<i>Hi, I can't come
to the phone right now.</i>

698
00:57:20,840 --> 00:57:22,239
<i>Please leave a message.</i>

699
00:57:23,560 --> 00:57:25,160
<i>Hi, Helene. It's me.</i>

700
00:57:25,880 --> 00:57:27,800
<i>I know you said you needed time,</i>

701
00:57:28,400 --> 00:57:31,280
<i>but I've found something very important
that you really need to hear.</i>

702
00:57:31,840 --> 00:57:33,360
<i>Call me as soon as you can.</i>

703
00:58:18,840 --> 00:58:20,359
-Thank you.
-Cheers.

704
00:58:20,360 --> 00:58:21,520
Cheers.

705
00:58:26,240 --> 00:58:28,160
You wanted to ask me something?

706
00:58:29,640 --> 00:58:31,840
Yes, um...

707
00:58:35,240 --> 00:58:36,240
Were...

708
00:58:37,880 --> 00:58:39,200
Were we separating?

709
00:58:41,480 --> 00:58:42,520
Sorry?

710
00:58:43,360 --> 00:58:47,799
Before I went missing, um...
Was divorce something we discussed?

711
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:49,239
Uh, what makes you say that?

712
00:58:49,240 --> 00:58:53,680
I just got this feeling. Like a flashback.

713
00:58:54,280 --> 00:58:55,320
A flashback?

714
00:58:56,040 --> 00:58:57,040
Mm-hmm.

715
00:58:58,000 --> 00:59:00,320
Okay? Pretty interesting.

716
00:59:04,160 --> 00:59:06,359
Mm... Were we divorcing?

717
00:59:06,360 --> 00:59:07,999
No! No.

718
00:59:08,000 --> 00:59:09,000
No.

719
00:59:10,480 --> 00:59:11,439
Okay.

720
00:59:11,440 --> 00:59:12,440
No way.

721
00:59:14,000 --> 00:59:17,399
Who is... Elisabeth Fauerskov?

722
00:59:17,400 --> 00:59:21,519
Um... She was the director
at one of our sub-contractors.

723
00:59:21,520 --> 00:59:25,279
Hm. And you knew her personally?

724
00:59:25,280 --> 00:59:28,840
Yes, I knew her from back in school.

725
00:59:30,480 --> 00:59:33,040
And do you know why she won't talk to me?

726
00:59:33,760 --> 00:59:35,039
You've lost me.

727
00:59:35,040 --> 00:59:37,959
She was one of the last people
I spoke to before I disappeared,

728
00:59:37,960 --> 00:59:40,040
so I phoned her today and um...

729
00:59:40,560 --> 00:59:42,559
She wouldn't talk to me at all.
She hung up, so...

730
00:59:42,560 --> 00:59:46,280
Okay, but there's actually a...
a simple reason for that. Um...

731
00:59:47,280 --> 00:59:53,759
We stopped working with them after...
they broke a trade-restraint clause,

732
00:59:53,760 --> 00:59:56,480
so she's not allowed
to speak to you by law.

733
00:59:59,480 --> 01:00:00,520
Oh.

734
01:00:01,760 --> 01:00:02,840
My love...

735
01:00:04,560 --> 01:00:08,560
Now please stop.
Don't embroil yourself with that again.

736
01:00:10,200 --> 01:00:13,839
You'll get tangled in a web of delusions
that lead to nowhere.

737
01:00:13,840 --> 01:00:16,199
-What?
-You're very upset.

738
01:00:16,200 --> 01:00:18,240
No, I'm not upset at all.

739
01:00:22,960 --> 01:00:24,520
Did we argue over her?

740
01:00:25,360 --> 01:00:28,880
Alexander told me we were arguing
before I disappeared, and...

741
01:00:29,640 --> 01:00:32,800
I thought perhaps we were arguing about
her and there was something going on?

742
01:00:33,360 --> 01:00:36,319
It's all in your mind.
I mean, Helene, you sound paranoid.

743
01:00:36,320 --> 01:00:38,639
I'm only asking a few questions here.

744
01:00:38,640 --> 01:00:39,640
Okay.

745
01:00:42,760 --> 01:00:48,360
I've tried saying it
as gently as possible, but I'll try again.

746
01:00:49,640 --> 01:00:51,120
You are ill, Helene.

747
01:00:55,560 --> 01:00:57,639
What are you trying to say?

748
01:00:57,640 --> 01:01:01,719
You have a form of personality disorder,
like schizophrenia.

749
01:01:01,720 --> 01:01:05,279
The doctors think
that maybe it's always been there...

750
01:01:05,280 --> 01:01:08,239
And um, the abrupt death
of your father triggered you.

751
01:01:08,240 --> 01:01:09,679
I am not schizophrenic.

752
01:01:09,680 --> 01:01:10,840
-Look...
-No!

753
01:01:13,640 --> 01:01:16,400
-So how do you explain it?
-Explain what?

754
01:01:17,720 --> 01:01:19,080
Helene, you left your family.

755
01:01:20,400 --> 01:01:26,119
You went to Norway. New name, new house.
You started a whole new life.

756
01:01:26,120 --> 01:01:27,879
Yeah, yeah, Edmund I had amnesia.

757
01:01:30,400 --> 01:01:33,959
Mm-hmm. From hitting your head?

758
01:01:33,960 --> 01:01:35,519
-Yes.
-Ah.

759
01:01:35,520 --> 01:01:37,999
Then you woke up on a ship.

760
01:01:39,560 --> 01:01:42,039
-Can you hear yourself?
-Yeah.

761
01:01:42,040 --> 01:01:46,239
It's not really a sane person
who does that, is it?

762
01:01:46,240 --> 01:01:48,519
I don't feel good. Um, I need air.

763
01:01:48,520 --> 01:01:51,079
-Here. Um, sit down.
-Can we go outside?

764
01:01:51,080 --> 01:01:52,879
-Take a breath. Breathe.
-No, I want...

765
01:01:52,880 --> 01:01:55,119
-Try to calm down.
-No, I just want some fresh air.

766
01:01:55,120 --> 01:01:57,199
I want some fresh air.
Will you please just...

767
01:01:59,800 --> 01:02:01,080
That's enough now!

768
01:02:04,600 --> 01:02:06,120
That's enough.

769
01:02:06,880 --> 01:02:11,039
Helene, I won't accept...
that you decimate our family again.

770
01:02:19,680 --> 01:02:22,640
It's okay. It's okay, it's okay...

771
01:02:24,840 --> 01:02:27,920
Come on, let's go upstairs.
You need to rest.

772
01:03:33,120 --> 01:03:36,759
-Hi. You okay?
-Hi there. I'm Joachim.

773
01:03:36,760 --> 01:03:39,359
-Joachim?
-Yes, uh, you know of me?

774
01:03:39,360 --> 01:03:40,759
-Yes. I do.
-Right.

775
01:03:40,760 --> 01:03:44,880
I just wanted to, um, speak to Helene.

776
01:03:48,720 --> 01:03:49,760
Um...

777
01:03:51,000 --> 01:03:52,640
Well, she's already gone to bed.

778
01:03:54,400 --> 01:03:56,999
-Okay. She's asleep already?
-Mm-hmm. Yes.

779
01:03:57,000 --> 01:04:01,240
Helene's gone through...
Well, quite a hard time.

780
01:04:01,960 --> 01:04:03,039
Mm.

781
01:04:03,040 --> 01:04:04,760
I'm... I'm sure she has.

782
01:04:05,440 --> 01:04:09,559
So if you want to talk to her,
might be best to come back another time.

783
01:04:09,560 --> 01:04:14,080
-Then I'll come back tomorrow to see her.
-I think she'll need more time than that.

784
01:04:15,200 --> 01:04:17,520
I'll have her get back to you
as soon as possible. Okay?

785
01:04:18,880 --> 01:04:20,360
But Joachim, um...

786
01:04:21,400 --> 01:04:23,759
Since you're already here...

787
01:04:23,760 --> 01:04:26,840
Uh, actually,
I'd love to speak to you about something.

788
01:04:27,320 --> 01:04:28,600
Have you got a minute?

789
01:04:30,360 --> 01:04:33,200
-Of course.
-Come in. Hmm?

790
01:04:41,680 --> 01:04:44,080
This is my mother, Caroline.

791
01:04:45,680 --> 01:04:46,800
Good evening.

792
01:04:47,800 --> 01:04:50,080
-Uh, let's go in here. Yeah?
-Sure.

793
01:04:56,640 --> 01:04:57,680
Joachim...

794
01:04:58,600 --> 01:05:01,879
-Is, um, is that for her? That folder?
-Yeah.

795
01:05:01,880 --> 01:05:04,160
-Mm-hmm.
-I've been trying to...

796
01:05:05,400 --> 01:05:07,599
Well, just kind of work it out.

797
01:05:07,600 --> 01:05:10,959
Yes. Of course.
Um, shall we look at it now, or...

798
01:05:10,960 --> 01:05:13,480
No, I'll talk directly with Helene, so...

799
01:05:18,480 --> 01:05:19,479
Joachim...

800
01:05:19,480 --> 01:05:21,399
Anything you'd like to ask me?

801
01:05:21,400 --> 01:05:24,360
Since you've been putting in
all that effort to...

802
01:05:25,520 --> 01:05:27,159
work it out, as you said.

803
01:05:27,160 --> 01:05:31,839
I was wondering why
you didn't go public when she...

804
01:05:31,840 --> 01:05:34,920
when she vanished. It's a bit... weird

805
01:05:35,800 --> 01:05:38,760
We were convinced that
Helene had ended it all.

806
01:05:39,600 --> 01:05:42,079
And I didn't want that
dragged through the press.

807
01:05:42,080 --> 01:05:45,639
Particularly for Alexander's sake.
He's our son.

808
01:05:45,640 --> 01:05:48,679
-And what about her father?
-What about him?

809
01:05:48,680 --> 01:05:52,639
The news of his death,
you also kept that news so quiet...

810
01:05:52,640 --> 01:05:54,520
-I would say.
-Yes, you're not wrong.

811
01:05:55,360 --> 01:05:58,239
It really was an unworthy death
for a man of his calibre.

812
01:05:58,240 --> 01:06:00,639
That's why we didn't go public with it.

813
01:06:00,640 --> 01:06:05,159
It's... so... fascinating.

814
01:06:05,160 --> 01:06:06,559
Fascinating?

815
01:06:06,560 --> 01:06:10,239
Well how do you do it?
There's nothing about any of you online.

816
01:06:10,240 --> 01:06:13,439
If you search, there's nothing.
It's like the whole family doesn't exist.

817
01:06:18,360 --> 01:06:23,440
Uh, yes.
Um, there's a reason for that as well.

818
01:06:25,480 --> 01:06:26,679
We had it erased.

819
01:06:26,680 --> 01:06:29,399
We have a department
in the company that handles that.

820
01:06:31,520 --> 01:06:32,719
But why?

821
01:06:32,720 --> 01:06:35,679
<i>We don't think
the tragedies of the Söderberg family</i>

822
01:06:35,680 --> 01:06:38,120
<i>should be a public spectacle.</i>

823
01:06:42,320 --> 01:06:45,279
Joachim, I understand
that this is hard for you.

824
01:06:45,280 --> 01:06:47,959
You've lost the woman that you love.

825
01:06:47,960 --> 01:06:52,599
What I can say is that
Helene always hurts people, unfortunately.

826
01:06:52,600 --> 01:06:54,519
Even if it's not her intention.

827
01:06:54,520 --> 01:06:57,279
That's why I have a proposal.

828
01:06:57,280 --> 01:06:58,720
Joachim...

829
01:07:00,320 --> 01:07:02,319
I gather you ran a café with her?

830
01:07:02,320 --> 01:07:05,719
Which is now closed?
Because you can't run it alone.

831
01:07:05,720 --> 01:07:11,240
I was also told that you've spent
several years working on a book too?

832
01:07:14,680 --> 01:07:15,999
Hang on, uh...

833
01:07:16,000 --> 01:07:18,919
I don't see how that's relevant,
to be honest with you...

834
01:07:18,920 --> 01:07:22,599
Joachim, I'll be blunt.
I have money that can help you.

835
01:07:25,240 --> 01:07:28,840
So I've had
an agreement drafted up. Um...

836
01:07:30,440 --> 01:07:35,240
Which, financially speaking,
is quite lucrative for you.

837
01:07:45,280 --> 01:07:46,199
CONFIDENTIALITY AGREEMENT

838
01:07:46,200 --> 01:07:48,439
We'd like to ensure
that Helene's disappearance,

839
01:07:48,440 --> 01:07:53,159
and the tragedy of our family
doesn't end up making it into a book

840
01:07:53,160 --> 01:07:54,919
or any kind of colourful story, you see.

841
01:07:56,160 --> 01:07:58,879
You and I have been through
some tragic events.

842
01:07:58,880 --> 01:08:02,600
But this has hurt Alexander most of all.
I've tried to shield him.

843
01:08:04,040 --> 01:08:06,440
And I intend to keep it that way.

844
01:08:09,640 --> 01:08:14,360
You can keep your hard-earned money,
'cause I'm gonna leave now.

845
01:08:18,040 --> 01:08:21,520
Uh, tell me. Are you under the influence?

846
01:08:23,960 --> 01:08:26,439
Perhaps you would like to sit down
for a little while.

847
01:08:26,440 --> 01:08:27,759
I haven't been drinking.

848
01:08:32,480 --> 01:08:33,840
You haven't had a drink?

849
01:08:35,680 --> 01:08:36,759
No.

850
01:08:36,760 --> 01:08:37,799
Okay.

851
01:08:39,600 --> 01:08:43,199
I'm not judging you. It would be
completely fair and understandable

852
01:08:43,200 --> 01:08:45,399
if you had felt the need
to have a drink today.

853
01:08:45,400 --> 01:08:47,759
-Well, I haven't. I've been fine.
-No?

854
01:08:47,760 --> 01:08:49,200
-Okay.
-Yeah.

855
01:08:51,040 --> 01:08:52,120
Goodbye.

856
01:08:53,240 --> 01:08:54,920
-You know your way out?
-Yeah.

857
01:09:21,320 --> 01:09:22,599
Joachim...

858
01:09:25,640 --> 01:09:27,320
Helene, what's wrong?

859
01:09:35,320 --> 01:09:37,120
Helene, come with me, darling.

860
01:09:38,960 --> 01:09:40,320
Let's get you back to bed.

861
01:09:42,920 --> 01:09:44,559
What are you saying?

862
01:09:44,560 --> 01:09:45,560
Edmund...

863
01:09:46,240 --> 01:09:47,240
Edmund?

864
01:09:48,440 --> 01:09:50,840
I know how he can be.

865
01:09:51,840 --> 01:09:53,200
But you know, Helene?

866
01:09:53,880 --> 01:09:58,400
After you vanished,
I'd not known him devastated like that.

867
01:09:59,640 --> 01:10:05,120
He loves you so much.
You and Alexander are everything to him.

868
01:10:06,440 --> 01:10:09,800
<i>Hi, I can't come to the phone
right now, please leave a message.</i>

869
01:11:17,880 --> 01:11:19,800
Get away. I hate you!

870
01:11:24,760 --> 01:11:26,000
Elisabeth?

871
01:12:02,920 --> 01:12:04,920
INBOX

872
01:12:17,080 --> 01:12:18,759
I'VE TRIED CALLING YOU
SEVERAL TIMES.

873
01:12:18,760 --> 01:12:20,520
IT'S IMPORTANT.
KIND REGARDS, ELISABETH

874
01:12:28,040 --> 01:12:29,040
Good morning.

875
01:12:29,760 --> 01:12:30,880
Good morning.

876
01:12:33,480 --> 01:12:35,119
-Okay, so you go first.
-Mm.

877
01:12:35,120 --> 01:12:37,680
-And no peeking. Mm.
-Uh-huh. Mm.

878
01:12:38,880 --> 01:12:40,119
Coffee.

879
01:12:41,680 --> 01:12:44,519
I need to take a call,
and then we'll go.

880
01:12:44,520 --> 01:12:45,560
It's your turn.

881
01:12:46,040 --> 01:12:49,199
-Right, and so I draw... A body?
-A body. You start there.

882
01:12:49,200 --> 01:12:50,239
Okay.

883
01:12:52,120 --> 01:12:53,839
Now it's your turn.

884
01:13:11,720 --> 01:13:12,760
All finished.

885
01:13:14,520 --> 01:13:15,559
Okay.

886
01:13:17,440 --> 01:13:19,320
Have a great day. Mm.

887
01:13:20,080 --> 01:13:24,760
And hey you, I love you. You are my life.

888
01:13:28,560 --> 01:13:29,560
What's wrong?

889
01:13:30,200 --> 01:13:32,840
It's just that's what you said
before you went away.

890
01:13:35,960 --> 01:13:39,720
Alexander, I won't leave you again, okay?

891
01:13:40,400 --> 01:13:42,960
I'll never leave you again. I swear.

892
01:13:43,560 --> 01:13:44,600
Never.

893
01:13:45,440 --> 01:13:46,480
Come here.

894
01:13:47,000 --> 01:13:49,679
-Mm. See you later.
-See ya.

895
01:13:49,680 --> 01:13:51,079
Go on, then.

896
01:13:51,080 --> 01:13:52,359
Yeah. Have fun.

897
01:13:52,360 --> 01:13:53,440
Bye.

898
01:13:54,320 --> 01:13:56,040
DYSSEGÅRD SCHOOL

899
01:14:16,480 --> 01:14:17,680
What's he doing here?

900
01:14:24,400 --> 01:14:26,359
I don't want you talking
to him any more.

901
01:14:26,360 --> 01:14:28,960
It might set you back
and I don't want you stressed.

902
01:14:31,360 --> 01:14:32,919
I know.

903
01:14:32,920 --> 01:14:36,279
But he won't go away
until I've said goodbye to him properly.

904
01:14:36,280 --> 01:14:40,040
I promise I'll end things with him,
for the sake of our family.

905
01:14:42,480 --> 01:14:43,480
Open it.

906
01:15:00,440 --> 01:15:02,159
Hi. I've been trying to reach you.

907
01:15:02,160 --> 01:15:05,039
I stopped by the house.
Did he speak to you about it?

908
01:15:05,040 --> 01:15:07,919
-There's so much you need to see.
-Joachim.

909
01:15:07,920 --> 01:15:10,280
-Joachim, stop. Stop it.
-I think he's hiding something...

910
01:15:10,720 --> 01:15:13,159
We can't about it. Not here.

911
01:15:13,160 --> 01:15:14,520
Are you scared of him?

912
01:15:15,280 --> 01:15:16,519
Helene, if he's hurt you...

913
01:15:16,520 --> 01:15:18,720
-I swear, I'm going to storm over...
-You can't. Stop.

914
01:15:22,320 --> 01:15:24,000
He has to think I'm finishing it.

915
01:15:26,080 --> 01:15:27,120
Okay?

916
01:15:30,320 --> 01:15:31,520
Please trust me.

917
01:15:36,640 --> 01:15:39,800
This is where I'm staying.
If you can make it there, we can talk.

918
01:15:42,360 --> 01:15:43,400
-Yeah.
-Okay.

919
01:15:44,040 --> 01:15:46,200
-Vi må sige farvel nu.
-Okay.

920
01:15:51,560 --> 01:15:56,200
You're right. Things don't add up.
But I'm figuring it out, okay?

921
01:15:57,360 --> 01:15:58,600
I love you.

922
01:16:01,000 --> 01:16:02,040
I love you.

923
01:16:33,440 --> 01:16:34,440
Yeah, okay.

924
01:17:18,040 --> 01:17:20,040
Yes, see you tomorrow then. Take care.

925
01:17:20,600 --> 01:17:24,839
Elisabeth, I need you to talk to me.
I'm not angry.

926
01:17:24,840 --> 01:17:25,759
What?

927
01:17:25,760 --> 01:17:28,639
Yeah, if you and Edmund are having
an affair and he dismissed you...

928
01:17:28,640 --> 01:17:31,799
Look I have no idea what's going on,
but, um, I'm just looking for answers.

929
01:17:31,800 --> 01:17:35,280
What are you talking about?
As if we're having an affair.

930
01:17:36,800 --> 01:17:38,399
Then why won't you speak to me?

931
01:17:38,400 --> 01:17:42,519
Because you lot forced me to sign a
legally-binding non-disclosure agreement!

932
01:17:42,520 --> 01:17:46,640
Um. Wait, wait, stop, please.
Stop. Who did?

933
01:17:47,280 --> 01:17:48,640
You know who did.

934
01:17:49,480 --> 01:17:51,360
-Your husband.
-Hang on.

935
01:17:53,160 --> 01:17:56,839
Okay. Um. Look, whatever...
I swear you can talk to me.

936
01:17:56,840 --> 01:17:59,759
Yeah, I've heard it all before.
"You won't do anything."

937
01:17:59,760 --> 01:18:01,559
I have no idea what you mean.

938
01:18:01,560 --> 01:18:04,120
If we've talked already,
I don't remember it.

939
01:18:05,400 --> 01:18:06,880
I don't remember it!

940
01:18:11,040 --> 01:18:13,639
Just over two years ago, you contacted me.

941
01:18:13,640 --> 01:18:15,640
And what I said then, is...

942
01:18:16,480 --> 01:18:20,200
that I'd found out that one of our ships
was being used to commit crimes.

943
01:18:20,720 --> 01:18:22,119
Serious stuff.

944
01:18:22,120 --> 01:18:24,920
Buying women. Human trafficking.

945
01:18:26,080 --> 01:18:27,840
Using your freight containers.

946
01:18:34,320 --> 01:18:37,720
Okay. And how did you discover it?

947
01:18:38,200 --> 01:18:41,960
I received emails from a woman
who said she had gathered some evidence.

948
01:18:42,640 --> 01:18:44,920
You know, photos of the containers.

949
01:18:45,600 --> 01:18:46,960
All the routes that were used.

950
01:18:47,600 --> 01:18:48,759
Schedules.

951
01:18:48,760 --> 01:18:50,999
She told me that it was systematic.

952
01:18:51,000 --> 01:18:54,400
And it wouldn't be going on
if someone high up hadn't approved it.

953
01:18:55,760 --> 01:18:59,800
She said she was working with the women
and she wanted to meet.

954
01:19:00,800 --> 01:19:02,639
So she then gave me an address.

955
01:19:02,640 --> 01:19:04,959
But before we could meet you contacted me.

956
01:19:04,960 --> 01:19:07,280
You said
that you would take it from there.

957
01:19:08,960 --> 01:19:10,319
Well, did we meet?

958
01:19:10,320 --> 01:19:12,719
I don't know.
I never heard from you again.

959
01:19:12,720 --> 01:19:15,160
And, well, I even thought that...

960
01:19:16,400 --> 01:19:17,880
you were actually behind it.

961
01:19:18,400 --> 01:19:19,720
It was a guess.

962
01:19:20,320 --> 01:19:24,039
I tried to talk to Edmund.
I tried to contact him about it.

963
01:19:24,040 --> 01:19:25,320
But he would just kill it.

964
01:19:26,400 --> 01:19:28,080
Our contract was cancelled.

965
01:19:28,760 --> 01:19:31,200
I was fired and forced to sign an NDA.

966
01:19:32,160 --> 01:19:34,960
And I was even threatened
by one of Edmund's employees.

967
01:19:35,680 --> 01:19:38,639
And I'm a single mum of two.
I couldn't risk it.

968
01:19:41,160 --> 01:19:43,080
That means they are still doing it.

969
01:19:43,600 --> 01:19:45,360
Yes. I'd say you're right.

970
01:19:46,280 --> 01:19:48,719
Do you still have her details
in your address book?

971
01:19:48,720 --> 01:19:51,719
Yes. She told me to meet here.

972
01:19:51,720 --> 01:19:54,040
-I think she worked there.
-Okay.

973
01:19:54,560 --> 01:19:58,159
Promise me you'll be careful if
you're beginning to dig this all up again.

974
01:19:58,160 --> 01:19:59,160
I will.

975
01:19:59,680 --> 01:20:02,319
And your contact, what was she called?

976
01:20:02,320 --> 01:20:03,680
Louise.

977
01:20:04,840 --> 01:20:06,079
Louise Andersen.

978
01:20:24,680 --> 01:20:27,120
NIGHTCLUB - GENTLEMENS CLUB

979
01:20:34,280 --> 01:20:35,239
Hi.

980
01:20:35,240 --> 01:20:36,240
Hi there.

981
01:20:36,840 --> 01:20:38,240
Can I help you?

982
01:20:38,800 --> 01:20:40,200
I'm looking for Louise.

983
01:20:42,520 --> 01:20:45,080
Sure, she won't be long. Go through.

984
01:21:01,440 --> 01:21:06,720
<i>♪ What was that tapping
On your window pane ♪</i>

985
01:21:07,520 --> 01:21:12,720
<i>♪ Started in the distance
But no sign of rain ♪</i>

986
01:21:14,200 --> 01:21:19,560
<i>♪ Shadows moving along the street ♪</i>

987
01:21:20,160 --> 01:21:25,280
<i>♪ You feel your heart
skip another beat... ♪</i>

988
01:21:27,200 --> 01:21:29,400
-Louise?
-Close. My name's Lulu.

989
01:21:30,240 --> 01:21:32,799
Do you want a drink? Champagne?

990
01:21:32,800 --> 01:21:35,039
Uh, no.
I'm looking for a girl called Louise.

991
01:21:35,040 --> 01:21:36,999
She worked here about two years ago.

992
01:21:37,000 --> 01:21:38,160
Order the champagne.

993
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:41,879
Yeah. Okay.

994
01:21:41,880 --> 01:21:44,080
A... A bottle of champagne, yeah.

995
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:47,680
<i>♪ And it's coming ♪</i>

996
01:21:49,760 --> 01:21:52,759
<i>♪ It's coming for you ♪</i>

997
01:22:05,200 --> 01:22:06,560
I hear you're looking for Louise?

998
01:22:07,760 --> 01:22:08,959
Champagne.

999
01:22:08,960 --> 01:22:11,400
Drink it.
Act like you're a normal customer.

1000
01:22:12,240 --> 01:22:14,040
What do you want with her?

1001
01:22:14,360 --> 01:22:15,680
Did you know her?

1002
01:22:16,320 --> 01:22:17,359
Yeah.

1003
01:22:17,360 --> 01:22:18,879
We used to work together.

1004
01:22:18,880 --> 01:22:20,959
-Do you know where she is?
-No.

1005
01:22:20,960 --> 01:22:24,000
I haven't seen her in... Two, three years.

1006
01:22:26,360 --> 01:22:28,120
What happened to her?

1007
01:22:30,080 --> 01:22:33,160
There was night after work
she told me she wasn't coming back here.

1008
01:22:33,840 --> 01:22:35,960
Well, did she tell you why that was?

1009
01:22:37,720 --> 01:22:38,840
She was afraid.

1010
01:22:40,800 --> 01:22:42,320
I don't know why.

1011
01:22:44,200 --> 01:22:48,600
Did she ever mention that she knew girls
who had been trafficked here?

1012
01:22:51,040 --> 01:22:54,279
All of us could say the same.
Most girls here at least.

1013
01:23:04,120 --> 01:23:05,400
Can I give you some advice?

1014
01:23:06,600 --> 01:23:07,919
You should be cautious.

1015
01:23:07,920 --> 01:23:10,040
People who ask questions like that
end up in trouble.

1016
01:23:13,440 --> 01:23:14,879
Wait, one last question.

1017
01:23:14,880 --> 01:23:16,799
Do... Do you know where she went?

1018
01:23:16,800 --> 01:23:19,279
Mm, she told me
she was leaving the country.

1019
01:23:19,280 --> 01:23:20,680
Something about going to Norway.

1020
01:25:49,040 --> 01:25:51,640
No! No!

1021
01:26:35,560 --> 01:26:36,800
What?

1022
01:26:37,440 --> 01:26:38,480
Huh. You're awake.

1023
01:26:39,200 --> 01:26:40,200
Where am I?

1024
01:26:43,520 --> 01:26:45,960
Uh, slowly. Take it easy.

1025
01:26:46,760 --> 01:26:48,400
Yeah. Just relax.

1026
01:26:50,360 --> 01:26:53,560
Helene, do you remember
how we discussed your medication?

1027
01:26:57,520 --> 01:26:58,520
Here you go.

1028
01:27:01,080 --> 01:27:02,320
You need to take two.

1029
01:27:04,800 --> 01:27:05,800
Mm.

1030
01:27:08,120 --> 01:27:09,120
Go ahead.

1031
01:27:11,160 --> 01:27:12,160
Mm.

1032
01:27:19,600 --> 01:27:21,280
Can I see? Open wide.

1033
01:27:23,880 --> 01:27:26,920
Helene, I've seen
every single trick in the book.

1034
01:27:40,600 --> 01:27:41,760
Good.

1035
01:28:02,040 --> 01:28:03,840
I had to.

1036
01:28:06,040 --> 01:28:07,600
I'm very sorry.

1037
01:28:09,040 --> 01:28:11,040
You just try and relax, okay?

1038
01:28:15,080 --> 01:28:16,919
Where's Alexander?

1039
01:28:16,920 --> 01:28:18,959
Well, he shouldn't see you like this.

1040
01:28:22,640 --> 01:28:24,000
What did you tell him?

1041
01:28:24,520 --> 01:28:26,639
I told him the truth.

1042
01:28:26,640 --> 01:28:28,959
I said that you're not well
and that you need rest.

1043
01:28:28,960 --> 01:28:29,919
He understood it.

1044
01:28:29,920 --> 01:28:31,360
He's aware you're sick.

1045
01:28:35,360 --> 01:28:37,679
I... I want to go home now.

1046
01:28:37,680 --> 01:28:40,160
-I want to go home to Alexander.
-I understand.

1047
01:28:41,040 --> 01:28:42,319
And we can do that.

1048
01:28:42,320 --> 01:28:44,840
But there's paperwork to deal with first.

1049
01:28:51,760 --> 01:28:53,839
APPOINTMENT OF GUARDIANSHIP

1050
01:28:56,800 --> 01:28:59,200
You... You want me under guardianship?

1051
01:29:00,200 --> 01:29:01,640
I'm trying to help.

1052
01:29:02,880 --> 01:29:04,919
I want you to have the best possible care.

1053
01:29:13,560 --> 01:29:16,640
Helene... I don't think you're listening.

1054
01:29:18,520 --> 01:29:20,880
This is for your own wellbeing. Hmm?

1055
01:29:24,760 --> 01:29:26,440
You can't run away again.

1056
01:29:29,240 --> 01:29:30,879
I know
what my father was trying to tell me.

1057
01:29:32,600 --> 01:29:34,280
And I know who Louise is.

1058
01:29:36,560 --> 01:29:39,160
-You won't get away with this, Edmund.
-Oh, my love...

1059
01:29:42,080 --> 01:29:46,760
You're seeing things you've imagined.
Things that aren't even real.

1060
01:29:52,680 --> 01:29:58,000
The pills will kick in soon. I've packed
some things for you to last a few days.

1061
01:29:58,880 --> 01:30:00,519
Try to get some rest.

1062
01:30:00,520 --> 01:30:03,600
I'll leave the papers here.
You can sign them when you feel better.

1063
01:30:10,880 --> 01:30:12,239
I love you.

1064
01:30:14,680 --> 01:30:17,120
Soon you'll be your old self again.

1065
01:30:53,720 --> 01:30:54,720
Hello!

1066
01:30:57,160 --> 01:30:58,520
Hello!

1067
01:30:59,320 --> 01:31:01,640
Let me out! I need to see my son!

1068
01:31:58,520 --> 01:31:59,920
We tried to escape.

1069
01:32:02,120 --> 01:32:03,240
<i>Helene!</i>

1070
01:32:06,800 --> 01:32:10,199
Helene! He's found us.

1071
01:32:11,320 --> 01:32:12,680
There's a ship

1072
01:32:14,520 --> 01:32:16,359
I think we can make it if we jump.

1073
01:32:16,360 --> 01:32:19,000
What, have you gone crazy?
We can't do that.

1074
01:32:34,680 --> 01:32:35,720
Damn it!

1075
01:33:02,960 --> 01:33:05,359
Ah! Come here!

1076
01:33:34,040 --> 01:33:37,679
They're looking for me.
Is there any way they'd know this address?

1077
01:33:37,680 --> 01:33:39,520
-No, no, no.
-Okay.

1078
01:33:40,880 --> 01:33:42,240
He has Alexander.

1079
01:33:43,320 --> 01:33:45,640
-I won't leave him there.
-We'll figure it out.

1080
01:33:46,360 --> 01:33:49,559
I knew her.
Louise Andersen. I met her.

1081
01:33:49,560 --> 01:33:50,479
Okay?

1082
01:33:50,480 --> 01:33:52,560
I was in contact with her, and she...

1083
01:33:53,040 --> 01:33:54,159
had evidence.

1084
01:33:54,160 --> 01:33:56,399
Proof that Edmund was using the company
for trafficking.

1085
01:33:56,400 --> 01:33:58,960
All right. Uh, tell me the whole story.

1086
01:34:00,960 --> 01:34:02,559
She fled to Norway. Um...

1087
01:34:02,560 --> 01:34:05,520
-Louise?
-Yes. And I followed her, and...

1088
01:34:07,400 --> 01:34:09,359
We... We were on a bridge, and I...

1089
01:34:09,360 --> 01:34:10,880
There was a bridge?

1090
01:34:11,520 --> 01:34:13,680
Where is it? Oh... damn.

1091
01:34:17,320 --> 01:34:18,360
Er det den?

1092
01:34:21,040 --> 01:34:24,199
I've been thinking a lot about that ship
and trying to figure out

1093
01:34:24,200 --> 01:34:26,399
how you got onto it if you didn't board
as a passenger,

1094
01:34:26,400 --> 01:34:28,200
and it's crazy, but what if you jumped?

1095
01:34:29,560 --> 01:34:33,360
And if you take the ship routes
and heights into account...

1096
01:34:33,840 --> 01:34:36,119
then this was the only place.

1097
01:34:36,120 --> 01:34:38,519
<i>Give me your bag and run.</i>

1098
01:34:38,520 --> 01:34:40,039
I'll stop him and speak to him.

1099
01:34:40,040 --> 01:34:42,799
-You can't! No way!
-You've done enough.

1100
01:34:42,800 --> 01:34:44,280
Give me your bag.

1101
01:34:49,560 --> 01:34:51,920
Run. Go!

1102
01:34:58,320 --> 01:34:59,320
Stop!

1103
01:35:02,040 --> 01:35:03,040
Stop!

1104
01:35:30,320 --> 01:35:31,920
Helene!

1105
01:35:36,320 --> 01:35:37,239
Helene...

1106
01:35:42,520 --> 01:35:43,520
Don't do it.

1107
01:35:52,840 --> 01:35:53,840
Helene...

1108
01:35:54,520 --> 01:35:57,359
I beg you. Don't do it.

1109
01:36:03,560 --> 01:36:04,640
It was Edmund.

1110
01:36:05,680 --> 01:36:11,280
He... He killed Louise.
And I saw it and then I... I jumped.

1111
01:36:18,400 --> 01:36:19,760
She gave me a...

1112
01:36:35,160 --> 01:36:37,160
Look at that...

1113
01:36:43,360 --> 01:36:46,120
-I kept it hidden.
-A little too hidden.

1114
01:36:51,960 --> 01:36:52,879
Hi.

1115
01:36:52,880 --> 01:36:56,280
-Helene?
-I need your help.

1116
01:36:58,920 --> 01:37:00,280
Found it.

1117
01:37:02,400 --> 01:37:04,359
What do we think we'll find on it?

1118
01:37:05,520 --> 01:37:06,800
Beviser af en slags.

1119
01:37:20,680 --> 01:37:24,120
My goodness. What is it?

1120
01:37:26,480 --> 01:37:27,520
Trafficking.

1121
01:37:33,160 --> 01:37:35,479
In our containers?

1122
01:37:35,480 --> 01:37:37,839
Yes. Edmund used my father's business.

1123
01:37:37,840 --> 01:37:40,519
So everything
that Elisabeth said was right.

1124
01:37:40,520 --> 01:37:41,639
Yes.

1125
01:37:41,640 --> 01:37:44,200
And then Edmund tried bury the evidence

1126
01:37:47,760 --> 01:37:49,400
-No.
-Hvad er der?

1127
01:37:49,920 --> 01:37:51,120
That ship...

1128
01:37:51,960 --> 01:37:54,239
We've been working with
the firm that owns that ship

1129
01:37:54,240 --> 01:37:55,879
for a long time.

1130
01:37:55,880 --> 01:37:57,920
From before Edmund joined the company.

1131
01:37:58,640 --> 01:37:59,640
Since when?

1132
01:38:07,760 --> 01:38:09,040
Over 50 years.

1133
01:38:15,080 --> 01:38:17,719
Weren't these the pages
that were torn from my book?

1134
01:38:17,720 --> 01:38:19,040
Uh, yes, I think so.

1135
01:38:24,080 --> 01:38:25,960
Helene, I have to tell you...

1136
01:38:26,560 --> 01:38:28,079
JM Shipping...

1137
01:38:28,080 --> 01:38:30,839
These were some of our partnerships
that your father handled.

1138
01:38:30,840 --> 01:38:33,159
He didn't want me to get involved in it.

1139
01:38:38,200 --> 01:38:39,519
CO-OPERATION FOR LIFE

1140
01:38:39,520 --> 01:38:40,880
{\an8}AKSEL SÖDERBERG
WITH J. M. SHIPPING

1141
01:38:44,480 --> 01:38:48,240
Edmund is probably involved
as well. It all points to that, but...

1142
01:38:49,000 --> 01:38:53,079
I'd say it started long before
he joined the firm, and there's no doubt.

1143
01:38:53,080 --> 01:38:56,120
So, my father started it?

1144
01:38:57,680 --> 01:38:58,720
Yeah.

1145
01:39:01,120 --> 01:39:03,239
So that's what he was trying to say...

1146
01:39:03,240 --> 01:39:06,279
Before he died,
he tried to confess, and warn me.

1147
01:39:06,280 --> 01:39:07,680
Edmund...

1148
01:39:14,880 --> 01:39:16,559
So, what now?

1149
01:39:16,560 --> 01:39:20,119
I need to get Alexander.

1150
01:39:20,120 --> 01:39:21,839
I must confront Edmund.

1151
01:39:21,840 --> 01:39:23,279
Yes, but Edmund is evil.

1152
01:39:23,280 --> 01:39:24,999
There's nothing he can do!
I have evidence.

1153
01:39:25,000 --> 01:39:28,279
So take that evidence to the police
so we can get out of this.

1154
01:39:28,280 --> 01:39:31,439
But we can't wait
for the police to look at it, Joachim.

1155
01:39:31,440 --> 01:39:33,559
They'll take months,
and he has a million lawyers,

1156
01:39:33,560 --> 01:39:35,680
and he can talk his way out of everything.

1157
01:39:36,320 --> 01:39:40,080
And yes, he is evil.
That's why I have to rescue Alexander.

1158
01:39:42,080 --> 01:39:45,520
"Should I leave the road
or go into the woods alone

1159
01:39:46,360 --> 01:39:48,559
when my mother has forbidden it."

1160
01:39:50,200 --> 01:39:52,119
-Mm?
-Grandma?

1161
01:39:52,120 --> 01:39:54,760
-Mm?
-Is Mum coming home?

1162
01:39:55,920 --> 01:39:58,240
Yes, I'm sure she'll soon be home again.

1163
01:40:00,760 --> 01:40:05,320
Don't you worry, darling.
Sleep tight. Good night.

1164
01:40:06,280 --> 01:40:08,160
-Goodnight.
-Goodnight.

1165
01:40:19,400 --> 01:40:21,240
She'll come home again.

1166
01:40:22,960 --> 01:40:24,000
Okay.

1167
01:40:25,760 --> 01:40:27,120
I'm going to bed.

1168
01:40:57,720 --> 01:41:00,560
Come and find me
if I'm not back in ten minutes.

1169
01:41:01,680 --> 01:41:02,760
Be safe.

1170
01:41:18,840 --> 01:41:23,000
Great to have you home again.
Would you like some wine?

1171
01:41:25,120 --> 01:41:27,960
I know what you and my father were doing.

1172
01:41:29,680 --> 01:41:31,160
I have proof now.

1173
01:41:31,760 --> 01:41:33,320
It's hidden in a safe place.

1174
01:41:34,840 --> 01:41:38,840
Alexander comes with me.
Let us go, and it stays hidden.

1175
01:41:41,080 --> 01:41:43,519
But we are leaving you.
And you have to let us.

1176
01:41:43,520 --> 01:41:47,480
Helene, you do not have a clue
what this is about.

1177
01:41:48,880 --> 01:41:52,000
I can't let you go.

1178
01:41:53,080 --> 01:41:57,520
In fact, I won't allow you
to disappear again.

1179
01:41:59,680 --> 01:42:00,840
Allow me to?

1180
01:42:04,880 --> 01:42:06,400
You let me disappear.

1181
01:42:07,400 --> 01:42:09,760
And you ensured that they found me again.

1182
01:42:10,280 --> 01:42:11,280
Okay.

1183
01:42:16,320 --> 01:42:20,840
It might be for the best if I explain
exactly what happened...

1184
01:42:22,360 --> 01:42:24,960
But afterwards,
I think you'll want to stay with me.

1185
01:42:26,240 --> 01:42:27,560
You're right.

1186
01:42:28,720 --> 01:42:31,600
You discovered
the company's involvement in trafficking

1187
01:42:32,160 --> 01:42:33,719
two years ago.

1188
01:42:33,720 --> 01:42:37,040
I wanted to stop you.
However, I couldn't stop you in time.

1189
01:42:37,800 --> 01:42:39,080
You got away.

1190
01:42:39,640 --> 01:42:43,400
At first, I thought you'd died in Norway.

1191
01:42:45,200 --> 01:42:48,680
But then I discovered
you started an entirely new life.

1192
01:42:49,600 --> 01:42:53,040
I had a hard time believing
the story about amnesia.

1193
01:42:54,520 --> 01:42:56,760
But in the end it was true.
Or was it?

1194
01:42:57,360 --> 01:42:58,400
Or was it?

1195
01:42:59,240 --> 01:43:00,640
Were you watching me?

1196
01:43:01,240 --> 01:43:02,840
Yeah.

1197
01:43:04,880 --> 01:43:06,360
Of course I was.

1198
01:43:07,520 --> 01:43:09,520
It became almost like an obsession.

1199
01:43:12,080 --> 01:43:13,920
And yet it really pained me...

1200
01:43:14,920 --> 01:43:16,000
to see you...

1201
01:43:16,760 --> 01:43:17,880
with him.

1202
01:43:36,160 --> 01:43:40,039
It wasn't easy for me
to see you living a life without me.

1203
01:43:40,040 --> 01:43:41,360
But I handled it.

1204
01:43:42,760 --> 01:43:44,799
Well, until it got too much for me.

1205
01:43:44,800 --> 01:43:48,359
I couldn't take seeing you
engaged to another man.

1206
01:43:48,360 --> 01:43:50,480
So I had to bring you home again.

1207
01:43:53,160 --> 01:43:54,480
Helene...

1208
01:43:58,280 --> 01:43:59,360
You're mine.

1209
01:44:05,760 --> 01:44:07,159
We belong together.

1210
01:44:15,960 --> 01:44:18,559
I knew that bringing
you home was a big risk.

1211
01:44:18,560 --> 01:44:21,599
It was a gamble to trust that
you wouldn't regain your memories,

1212
01:44:21,600 --> 01:44:24,040
which was, of course, naive.

1213
01:44:26,080 --> 01:44:29,400
You let our son live
without his mother for two years.

1214
01:44:32,000 --> 01:44:34,000
But I did let you live, Helene.

1215
01:44:49,640 --> 01:44:51,799
What about Louise?
You didn't let her live.

1216
01:44:51,800 --> 01:44:53,520
-No.
-You killed her.

1217
01:44:54,680 --> 01:44:57,800
-She was ruining what we had.
-You're insane.

1218
01:45:01,160 --> 01:45:02,240
I love you.

1219
01:45:03,760 --> 01:45:06,479
I love you more than anything
in this world.

1220
01:45:06,480 --> 01:45:08,880
I'm going to get Alexander.

1221
01:45:09,960 --> 01:45:11,560
And you'll let us go.

1222
01:45:12,200 --> 01:45:14,039
-No.
-Yes, you will.

1223
01:45:14,040 --> 01:45:16,439
-No.
-You're going to, I have evidence!

1224
01:45:16,440 --> 01:45:18,919
The proof you have
mainly implicates your father,

1225
01:45:18,920 --> 01:45:20,440
and he's not here to contest it.

1226
01:45:21,080 --> 01:45:23,960
So then who takes the fall? Our company.

1227
01:45:24,640 --> 01:45:28,120
And our company, my love...
That's you and me.

1228
01:45:28,680 --> 01:45:30,759
Hi, Ingrid.
I wanted to ask you about something.

1229
01:45:30,760 --> 01:45:33,759
That book you showed us
with old employees?

1230
01:45:33,760 --> 01:45:36,879
-<i>yes?</i>
-In the photo from 1976.

1231
01:45:36,880 --> 01:45:40,799
There's a tall blonde lady in the line.
She looks familiar.

1232
01:45:40,800 --> 01:45:44,079
If you go to the police,
I'll take you down with me.

1233
01:45:44,080 --> 01:45:46,959
So how about we just sort this out
as a family?

1234
01:45:46,960 --> 01:45:49,799
-Don't come near me.
-Don't shout, you'll wake Alexander up.

1235
01:45:49,800 --> 01:45:53,320
<i>The woman on the left.
That's Caroline, Edmund's mother.</i>

1236
01:45:54,680 --> 01:45:56,360
Mother, can you sort her out?

1237
01:46:04,760 --> 01:46:06,799
And did she work at the company?

1238
01:46:06,800 --> 01:46:10,240
<i>Yes. She was Aksel Söderberg's secretary
before me.</i>

1239
01:46:26,160 --> 01:46:27,559
You can't treat me like this!

1240
01:46:27,560 --> 01:46:29,479
Come back!
Don't you walk away from me!

1241
01:46:29,480 --> 01:46:32,480
-Get off me! Get away! I hate you!
-Hey! Wait!

1242
01:46:33,280 --> 01:46:35,519
This is what happens
when you treat me like this.

1243
01:46:35,520 --> 01:46:37,520
Stop this. Caroline!

1244
01:46:40,960 --> 01:46:42,400
It was you.

1245
01:46:44,080 --> 01:46:46,199
You were here, when I was little.

1246
01:46:46,200 --> 01:46:48,360
Get her upstairs or she'll wake Alexander.

1247
01:46:56,240 --> 01:46:58,359
Put her on the bed.

1248
01:46:58,360 --> 01:47:00,439
-Let go.
-Easy.

1249
01:47:00,440 --> 01:47:02,760
Easy, easy, easy.

1250
01:47:04,520 --> 01:47:07,200
Okay. Okay.

1251
01:47:07,800 --> 01:47:11,279
Why were you here back then?
You said you didn't know my father well.

1252
01:47:11,280 --> 01:47:14,280
Helene, your father was a bad man.

1253
01:47:15,640 --> 01:47:16,799
What are you talking about?

1254
01:47:16,800 --> 01:47:18,800
For eight years, I looked after him.

1255
01:47:20,080 --> 01:47:22,080
I loved him. Worshipped him.

1256
01:47:22,680 --> 01:47:24,280
He said he loved me as well.

1257
01:47:25,120 --> 01:47:26,840
He promised we'd get married.

1258
01:47:27,400 --> 01:47:29,199
But as soon as he met your mother,

1259
01:47:29,200 --> 01:47:32,720
he broke it off with me for her.
He cast me out.

1260
01:47:33,480 --> 01:47:35,079
I wasn't good enough any longer.

1261
01:47:35,080 --> 01:47:39,039
-<i>What's your emergency?
-</i> Hi. I think I need some help here.

1262
01:47:39,040 --> 01:47:41,880
<i>-What's your location?</i>
-Could you send the police to, uh...

1263
01:47:42,520 --> 01:47:44,239
-Lindevej 12.
<i>-Yes, of course.</i>

1264
01:47:44,240 --> 01:47:46,040
<i>Can you tell me what this is about?</i>

1265
01:47:57,160 --> 01:48:02,040
He underestimated mother
and how much she knew about his secrets.

1266
01:48:02,760 --> 01:48:06,200
I had to make sure
Edmund had a future at Söderberg

1267
01:48:06,880 --> 01:48:08,279
We deserved it.

1268
01:48:08,280 --> 01:48:11,679
So I forced Aksel to hire Edmund.

1269
01:48:11,680 --> 01:48:15,240
But Helene, you have to believe me.
Our love...

1270
01:48:16,440 --> 01:48:17,920
It was always real.

1271
01:48:29,680 --> 01:48:31,519
You two are sick.

1272
01:48:31,520 --> 01:48:33,679
You see? I told you she'd react this way.

1273
01:48:33,680 --> 01:48:34,999
She just needs a bit more time.

1274
01:48:35,000 --> 01:48:37,760
Last time you let her live
you saw what happened!

1275
01:48:38,280 --> 01:48:40,560
You know she has to die,
just like her father.

1276
01:48:41,160 --> 01:48:43,720
So that everything
we've fought for isn't ruined.

1277
01:48:44,960 --> 01:48:48,720
Dad? Dad? Dad? Dad?

1278
01:48:53,160 --> 01:48:56,799
You killed my father
to stop him confessing?

1279
01:48:56,800 --> 01:49:00,680
Remarkable how you find your morality
when close to death, wouldn't you say?

1280
01:49:11,720 --> 01:49:13,120
You're going to have to finish it.

1281
01:49:13,760 --> 01:49:16,279
-I'll get her to come around.
-No, Edmund!

1282
01:49:16,280 --> 01:49:21,039
You insisted on bringing Helene home
and I let you, but it didn't work, okay?

1283
01:49:21,040 --> 01:49:22,159
So this stops here!

1284
01:49:22,160 --> 01:49:23,439
Mother!

1285
01:49:28,200 --> 01:49:29,879
It is my decision.

1286
01:49:29,880 --> 01:49:31,680
You're pathetic.

1287
01:49:32,360 --> 01:49:35,120
This is pathetic. She doesn't want you,
don't you see that?

1288
01:49:35,760 --> 01:49:37,360
Don't you see that?

1289
01:49:39,800 --> 01:49:41,040
Fine, I'll do it.

1290
01:49:42,920 --> 01:49:46,360
Stop! Stop! Mother, stop it! Stop it now!

1291
01:49:46,840 --> 01:49:48,319
Stop! Stop, hey!

1292
01:49:48,320 --> 01:49:50,400
She's still Alexander's mother!

1293
01:49:53,560 --> 01:49:55,160
No!

1294
01:49:57,160 --> 01:49:58,640
No. No...

1295
01:50:02,400 --> 01:50:04,480
Mother... Mother...

1296
01:50:05,480 --> 01:50:07,960
Mother... Mother...

1297
01:50:10,960 --> 01:50:13,000
No. No.

1298
01:50:41,480 --> 01:50:44,600
Mother! Mother!

1299
01:50:46,880 --> 01:50:50,720
Mother... No. No.

1300
01:52:12,760 --> 01:52:15,479
<i>Traffic police
have been notified.</i>

1301
01:52:15,480 --> 01:52:18,999
<i>An ambulance is on the way
to the crime scene, ETA 20 minutes.</i>

1302
01:52:30,240 --> 01:52:31,240
Yes, it is!

1303
01:52:33,200 --> 01:52:35,839
You see? See that white house there?

1304
01:52:35,840 --> 01:52:38,839
-Yeah.
-With the swimming pier? You see it?

1305
01:52:38,840 --> 01:52:40,239
Will we live there?

1306
01:52:40,240 --> 01:52:41,800
If you'd like to.

1307
01:52:43,680 --> 01:52:45,439
-Come on, Mummy!
-Whoo!

1308
01:52:45,440 --> 01:52:47,879
-Here she comes!
-Yeah.

1309
01:52:47,880 --> 01:52:49,280
Oh, it's cold!

1310
01:52:51,960 --> 01:52:54,399
-I'm gonna spin you. Go on.
-All right.

1311
01:52:54,400 --> 01:52:56,479
Here we go!

1312
01:52:58,280 --> 01:53:00,679
Ah!

1313
01:53:00,680 --> 01:53:02,639
Okay, again! Come on!

1314
01:53:02,640 --> 01:53:05,239
Throw it to me over there
and then I'll swim over.

1315
01:53:05,240 --> 01:53:06,959
Great. You gonna swim under?

1316
01:53:06,960 --> 01:53:10,519
Yeah I'll swim under,
and then I'll come back to you, okay?

1317
01:53:10,520 --> 01:53:11,599
Throw it to me.

1318
01:53:11,600 --> 01:53:13,599
-Oh!
-Okay, are you ready?

1319
01:53:13,600 --> 01:53:14,559
Yeah.

1320
01:53:14,560 --> 01:53:17,080
Okay. Three, two, one. Throw!

1321
01:53:17,720 --> 01:53:19,519
No, further than that!

1322
01:53:19,520 --> 01:53:21,800
Hey, Mum, it's really great here!

1323
01:53:23,040 --> 01:53:25,600
You always did like swimming.

1324
01:53:26,640 --> 01:53:28,400
Can you remember now?

1325
01:53:29,000 --> 01:53:30,560
A few things, yes.
